enerate"] ["text" "star"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069697/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba9afb75fe1614ba99a695afee9db33f34ecd22abed6b76f367b1e2fbcc0f784"} {"question" "q-333672" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "star"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069697/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba9afb75fe1614ba99a695afee9db33f34ecd22abed6b76f367b1e2fbcc0f784"} {"question" "q-333678" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. Select the correct options below regarding the given system.$\\,$ The equilibrium point (origin) is a \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\nnode." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069697/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba9afb75fe1614ba99a695afee9db33f34ecd22abed6b76f367b1e2fbcc0f784"} {"question" "q-333678" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix of our system is\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that:\n\n- Since the only (repeated) eigenvalue of $A$ is $\\lambda =-1$ and it's negative, we have a $\\text{stable}$ node.\n\n- Since $A$ is diagonal and has a repeated eigenvalue, there are infinitely many linearly independent eigenvectors. So, we have a $\\text{star}$ node.\n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069697/assets/92efcce675a436ad349ca6139cb12cda88fbdd5bdeaf2a5f1e755e7ba1f6d037.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mat